description.en:
From March to May 1933 Chinese forces defended the Great Wall passes. Main units:

- Xifengkou and Luowenyu: 29th Army (Song Zheyuan), with the 37th Division (Feng Zhi’an), 38th Division (Zhang Zizhong), and Provisional 2nd Division (Liu Ruming);
- Gubeikou and Nantianmen: Northeast Army’s 67th Corps (Wang Yizhe) held first, reinforced by the Central Army’s 17th Army (Xu Tingyao) with the 2nd Division (Huang Jie), 25th Division (Guan Linzheng), and 83rd Division (Liu Kan);
- Lengkou: 32nd Army (Shang Zhen), including the 139th Division;
- Jielingkou: Northeast Army’s 53rd Corps (Wan Fulin) and others.

Hampered by inferior equipment and coordination, the Chinese forces eventually withdrew, and the Tanggu Truce was signed on 31 May.

Dates and unit designations follow conventional accounts and await historical review.
